{
  "$comment": "Build input, not documentation. The rule is TRD Section 7: a component is client-only if its public props include a function, or if it uses state, effects, refs, or browser APIs internally. Everything else is server-capable and carries NO directive. check-client-boundary.mjs fails on any exported component missing from this file, so a new component cannot ship unclassified.",
  "rule": "client if public props include a function, or it uses state/effects/refs/browser APIs; else server",
  "trdSection": "7",
  "special": {
    "Table": "Static parts are server-capable; interactive parts (sort, select, resize) are client.",
    "Alert": "Non-dismissible is server-capable; a dismissible Alert takes onDismiss and is therefore client.",
    "ClaraProvider": "Client-only: resolves the system colour-scheme preference in an effect, and holds context state.",
    "ButtonGroup": "Client-only: roving tabindex needs state and a DOM effect (US-01M0GM3S AC1).",
    "Field": "Client-only, reclassified during implementation: Field renders a context Provider, and a Server Component cannot - so it and every control reading that context are client-only. The context object itself lives in lib/, not components/, because it is infrastructure rather than a component and does not belong in this classification.",
    "Checkbox": "Client-only: `indeterminate` is a DOM property that must be set in an effect."
  },
